  "bo_system": "Idox Uniform",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development by virtue of its overall size and bulkiness of roof form, its excessive width and detailed design, particularly when viewed in conjunction with the proposed large rear dormer and first floor rear extension, would appear visually intrusive, incongruous, overly dominant and out of keeping with the character and appearance of the host building and the surrounding area of which it forms part. The proposal is therefore contrary to Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D4, D5 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD6, DMD11, DMD13 and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its inadequate functional floor area due to the low floor-to-ceiling heights, and inadequate outlook and light to bedroom 2 would result in substandard and inappropriate accommodation incapable of meeting the reasonable needs of occupiers contrary to Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), to Policies D3 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), to Policies CP4 and CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), to Policies DMD5 and DMD8 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), and the Housing Design Standards London Plan Guidance (2023).",
    "The proposed development, by virtue of the overprovision of car parking spaces, the absence of a swept path analysis and visibility splays, and the obstructive siting and and inappropriate location of refuse and cycle storage, would result in a poor-quality parking layout that would impede safe ingress and egress, compromise manoeuvrability for vehicles (including emergency and servicing vehicles), and obstruct visibility for pedestrians and other road users, contrary to Section 9 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy T6.1 of the London Plan (2021), Policies DMD 8, DMD 45 and DMD 47 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), Policies CP24 and CP25 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010).",
    "The proposal would not offer a mechanism to deliver the statutory Biodiversity Net Gain. The proposal would therefore contrary to Schedule 7A of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (inserted by the Environment Act 2021), Section 16 of National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy G6 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP36 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010) and Policies DMD78 and DMD 79 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed development with inadequate Flood Risk Assessment and source control SuDS measures fails to demonstrate that the proposed development would both be safe from flooding; will not increase flood risk elsewhere or demonstrate measures to manage the risk of flooding from surface water run-off and follow the drainage hierarchy in the London Plan. This is contrary to guidance in Section 14 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024); Policies SI 12 and SI 13 of the London Plan (2021); Policy CP28 of the Core Strategy (2010) and Policies DMD59, DMD60 and DMD61 of the Development Management Document (2014)."
  ],
